{"entryId":"2275","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:2275:1","sourceSha256":"c1dc702847ef89cc85b758b362bd33fdb045250056ffece0551336b7ce16c002","englishSha256":"0e74807d9b9a412443fa97e5e32bdc66625d0813b389e7ff51d5b816a92aefbf","citations":[{"id":"2275:1:link-01","he":[96,110],"en":[137,150],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_57b.2"},"reference":"Nedarim 57b:2","assessment":"Both toponyms and the visits to Ammi and Yitzḥak Nappaḥa are present. The passage begins as a question about the case of an onion replanted after the Sabbatical year.","evidence":[{"reference":"Nedarim 57b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_57b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Nedarim 57b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_57b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"Both toponyms and the visits to Ammi and Yitzḥak Nappaḥa are present. The passage begins as a question about the case of an onion replanted after the Sabbatical year.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The Bavli explicitly introduces the issue as a question and records Ammi’s inability to answer it.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Nedarim 57b:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_57b.2"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Nedarim 57b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Nedarim_57b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]}],"entryEvidence":[]}
